0..64 Comment "// A reflexivity at a point composes with `Path.step` in a type."
65..67 Comment "//"
68..149 Comment "// `Path.here(x)` reads its type off its point\'s binder, whatever type the binder"
150..227 Comment "// writes: `Path(A, x, x)` when `x : A`. A composite whose first operand is a"
228..293 Comment "// reflexivity, or ends in one, takes its type from that reading."
294..296 Comment "//"
297..357 Comment "// Each declaration states such a composite in its own type."
358..360 Comment "//"
361..431 Comment "// - see: #3834 — a reflexivity first in a composite, refused before"
433..508 Comment "/// A reflexivity stands first in the type\'s composite. The left unit holds"
509..585 Comment "/// up to a path, not by computation, so the composite stands on both sides."
586..589 Keyword "def"
590..599 FunctionDef "hereFirst"
